Join code fj-abcd1234, valid once until 14:05 (core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766).
On the new machine, paste one line:

Natively, one agent per machine: it can run FrIDE instances, keep backups and become
the core. The line installs Tailscale and fridolin, and asks before it changes anything:
  macOS, Linux (sh):
    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/fridolin/COMMIT/container/node.sh | sh -s -- --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 --code fj-abcd1234
  Windows (PowerShell):
    & ([scriptblock]::Create((irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/fridolin/COMMIT/container/node.ps1))) -Core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 -Code fj-abcd1234

In a box (Docker), the fallback where Docker Sandboxes can't run, e.g. a machine
without virtualization:
  macOS, Linux (sh):
    curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/fridolin/COMMIT/container/box.sh | sh -s -- --registry ghcr.io/owner --version abcd1234 --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 --code fj-abcd1234
  Windows (PowerShell):
    & ([scriptblock]::Create((irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OWNER/fridolin/COMMIT/container/box.ps1))) -Registry ghcr.io/owner -Version abcd1234 -Core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766 -Code fj-abcd1234

With fridolin installed already:
  macOS, Linux (sh):
    fridolin node join fj-abcd1234 --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766
  Windows (PowerShell):
    & "$env:ProgramFiles\fridolin\fridolin.exe" node join fj-abcd1234 --core fridolin-core.example.ts.net:8766

Add --root PATH[:rw] to share a folder, --no-exec to allow no commands (docs/NODES.md);
node.ps1 takes them as -Root PATH[:rw] and -NoExec.
Then approve it here: fridolin nodes approve <id>, and fridolin nodes approve <id> --commands
